{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs",
  "item": "impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[outgoing_edges]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Domain requires this callback even for a storage-only consumer. The\n delegation test must use only node_path; discovering edges would be\n an unwanted graph access, which this guard rejects. Traversal fixtures\n separately exercise edge discovery."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs#impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[outgoing_edges]` is a valid coverage exception.\n\n- **Form.** It is written as fenced citation commentary on an explicit function with a body. It gives a prose reason rather than citing difficulty alone.\n- **Reason is substantive.** The method only panics, as a guard. The `Domain` trait requires the callback, but this storage-only fixture must not discover edges.\n- **Agrees with the source.** `StoredGraph::node_path` is the only `Domain` method that `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` call, so the delegation test never reaches the guard. Those methods are `consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path`, which exercises them, and `malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors`, whose `StoredReview::execute` does no edge discovery.\n- **Claim about other fixtures.** Other fixtures do implement and exercise `outgoing_edges`, for example `Memory` in `src/graph/validation_tests.rs` and `Memory` in `src/agent/tests.rs`. This supports \"Traversal fixtures separately exercise edge discovery\".\n- **No other citation.** The item carries no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference that would make the citation redundant.",
